  "limitations": [
    "Reviewed by a fresh read-only `codex exec` invoked by hand, not by `xtask review`: the controller's predecessor gate refuses P09 subjects until C26 completes; D058 and the owner's 2026-10-26 instruction authorise proceeding. Receipts are regenerated through the controller once C26 completes.",
    "The working tree holds the owner's uncommitted C26 attempt-02 and academy-2.1 work, excluded from scope; the input inventory covers the compiled and tested sources.",
    "`xtask check`/`xtask test` as whole commands were not run (they would include the owner's in-progress work); their constituent commands relevant to this chunk were run individually with exit codes and log hashes recorded.",
    "The chunk's work is committed on branch c42-academy at HEAD (the pre-gate commit 6a42a9fa and the attempt-01 remediation commit: Your place through a PlaceContext (R1), the paths row on tRPC's own paths.list query key holding the raw reply (R2), the real path page asserted with contract-shaped paths.get fixtures in the suite and the synthetic catalog and by the driver (R3/E1), an explicit judgement of the composites in parity/notes.md (E2); and the attempt-02 remediation commit (reviews/C42/remediation-attempt-02.md): the Learning paths row rereads paths.list when a units.complete or units.submitKnowledgeCheck mutation settles in the generation's cache, on error as a readback without replay (R2), with a production-provider regression through a unit completion (first receipt lost), a second completion and a knowledge-check submission; run-checks.sh's fixture-command label corrected; themeFor pinned. and the attempt-03 remediation commit (reviews/C42/remediation-attempt-03.md): desktop.attempt.submit counts as a progress mutation so a passed desktop lab or an uncertain submission rereads the row (R2, with a production-provider regression through the real lab runner), the card's summary is the contract's tagline and both fixtures carry it (R3). Attempt-04 scored 9/9/9/8/8 with no required fixes or evidence gaps; its one blocker (B1) is the predecessor record, now present: C41's review record is docs/planning/reviews/C41/attempt-01 in the c41-api worktree (read it). C42 consumes C41's pre-gate commit 70b4a920 by design: every P09 chunk is reviewed on its own worktree branched from its predecessor's pre-gate commit, predecessor remediation is integrated by the merge chain into main and validated by the P09 phase review on the integrated tree (docs/planning/p09-recut.md; the owner's dependency amendment of 2026-10-30, recorded in reviews/C42/remediation-attempt-03.md). The tagline is now asserted inside the Learning paths card (suite and driver). Attempt-05 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers and was accepted at 8 under D034 (reviews/C42/attempt-05/acceptance.md); its failures are remediated in the attempt-05 remediation commit (reviews/C42/remediation-attempt-05.md): the shell's ink-on-accent focus ring is scoped to the accent-filled sidebar destination so the Academy's section links keep the accent ring (5.05:1 light, 4.86:1 dark on the soft surface; R1, with a stylesheet-scope regression), and N02 measures the selected and an unselected section link in both themes against a plain capture focused on the page heading, requiring a ring with a median contrast of at least 3:1 against the surface it replaces (R2, E1); the Rust paths.list fixture says tagline; BASE_REF=70b4a920) in its own worktree branched from C41's commit 70b4a920 (on c41-api, itself from C40's 73048f76, C39b's 49a5bac1, C39a's 640103e7 and main's C38 1ff6fe17), so the earlier chunks' gates stayed in scope; scope and diff.patch are measured from 70b4a920. The owner's uncommitted build files (xtask sources, Cargo.lock, the Tauri manifests, the desktop-core version bump, the harness pin, the legacy feature views) are present as uncommitted copies, excluded from scope as the owner's work; the v2 Academy imports no legacy view (AcademyView is not imported; the learner provider and the offline work under features/academy are shared infrastructure until C44). Native acceptance C42-N01..N02 recorded against the rebuilt fixture bundle (native-prepare.json; executable hash bound in native-acceptance.json) with AX trees, self-captures and the measured layout matrix under evidence/C42/screens, against the synthetic Academy endpoint (academy_server.py) with the device sign-in granted. The owner's dependency amendment of 2026-10-30 applies (approved in the owner's words, \"Dependency amendment approved\"): P09 chunks are reviewed on their own worktrees from each predecessor's pre-gate commit; predecessor remediation is integrated by the merge chain and validated by the P09 phase review, so a chunk's review takes the predecessor's record as it stands.",
    "Visual parity (D059, docs/planning/p09-recut.md): the composites under docs/planning/evidence/C42/parity (prototype board left, fixture app right, captured by the native script from the signed-in catalog state) are posted with their deviations; the composite is judged on the chrome, the embed's content is the Academy's own (P19); parity/notes.md records the owner's explicit approval of both composites with their deviations on 2026-10-30 (C42",
